    "created_at": "2025-02-14T01:00:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-14T01:00:39Z",
    "body": "FWIW, and with a big disclaimer that I'm not a native English speaker, I always assumed \"channel\" was about a full color layer of the bitmap, certainly because I did some silk printing when I was young and because Photoshop calls it like that. Whereas I see \"component\" as referring to what makes a `<color>` value. \nSo, for me, \"*the red component of an image*\" sounds weird, while \"*the red channel of an image*\" is clear, and, \"*the red channel of the `<color>` `rgb(100%, 0%, 0%)`*\" also sounds weird, here I'd use \"component\".  \nWhere it's getting complicated with this definition is when we talk about \"a pixel\", where both can make sense depending if the pixel is considered a part of a bitmap, or something on its own made of numerical values (I believe we have both in HTML).\n",
